# A tetrahedron with two materials, written by hand.
#
# The baker's only end-to-end check, and it is checked in for a reason no test file explains
# by itself: every real model this repository has ever been pointed at is somebody else's
# download, tens of megabytes, and not ours to redistribute — so `models/` is ignored and a
# clone has nothing to bake. Two sessions lost an afternoon each to faults nothing but a real
# bake could see (a zip holds raw deflate while the reader called zlib inflate; a depth blit
# refuses a format mismatch), and `npm run typecheck` covering `scripts/` still cannot find
# that class of thing. Running the tool can.
#
# Four vertices, four faces, two materials, one shared normal set, and UVs — enough that the
# reader has to resolve an .mtl, group faces by material, and emit more than one surface.
# Small enough to read in full in a diff.

mtllib tetra.mtl

v 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 1.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 1.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 0.000000 1.000000

vt 0.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 0.000000
vt 0.000000 1.000000

vn 0.000000 0.000000 -1.000000
vn 0.000000 -1.000000 0.000000
vn -1.000000 0.000000 0.000000
vn 0.577350 0.577350 0.577350

usemtl shell
f 1/1/1 3/3/1 2/2/1
f 1/1/2 2/2/2 4/3/2
f 1/1/3 4/2/3 3/3/3

usemtl core
f 2/1/4 3/2/4 4/3/4
